## Build and Test — Kiro와 동일 (steering/02 · 04)

| 서브에이전트 | 역할 | 단축키 | 설정 파일 |
|-------------|------|--------|-----------|
| `qa-tester` | 빌드·테스트·진단 (Anti-Bias) | Ctrl+Shift+5 | `qa-tester.json` |
| `tmf-compliance-reviewer` | TMF-01~TMF-09 검증 | Ctrl+Shift+6 | `tmf-compliance-reviewer.json` |
| `web-integration-tester` | API 스키마 + Playwright E2E | Ctrl+Shift+7 | `web-integration-tester.json` |

### 흐름 (Kiro steering/02와 동일)

```text
Code Generation 완료 (대상 Unit)
  │
  ▼
병렬 가능: qa-tester | tmf-compliance-reviewer | web-integration-tester
  ├─ FAIL → fix-request → 해당 codegen 에이전트 위임 → 재검증 (최대 3회)
  └─ 전체 PASS → Build and Test 완료
```

### 피드백 루프 (Kiro와 동일)

1. **qa-tester / tmf-compliance-reviewer / web-integration-tester는 코드를 수정하지 않음** (읽기·실행·분석만)
2. 실패 시 fix-request → codegen 에이전트 위임
3. 최대 3회 반복 후 에스컬레이션
4. **체크박스·audit.md는 메인 에이전트가 수행**


## Remote MCP (Jira / GitLab MR)

The main agent records approval markers in the audit log and performs or sequences `jira_*` and `gitlab_create_merge_request` MCP calls per `aidlc-requirements-analysis`, `aidlc-code-generation`, and `aidlc-build-and-test`. When using `Task` to delegate, ensure the main thread writes the markers required by `.cursor/rules/workflow.mdc` (**Remote workflow gates**) before the subagent invokes remote MCP, or keep remote MCP on the main thread.

## Build and Test — FAIL feedback (codegen delegation)

- `qa-tester`, `tmf-compliance-reviewer`, and `web-integration-tester` **must not** modify product code (analyze / run / report only).
- When a gate is **FAIL**, the **main** agent creates `aidlc-docs/construction/{unit}/build-and-test/fix-request-{unit}.md`, then invokes **Task** for the matching Kiro codegen agent (`codegen-backend`, `codegen-db`, `codegen-frontend`, or `codegen-iac`) per `.unicli-rules/construction/build-and-test.md`. Re-run the failed gate(s). Stop after **three** failed remediation cycles and escalate to the user.
- Each Task must load `.kiro/agents/prompts/{agent_name}.md` first, then align with `.cursor/skills/{agent_name}/SKILL.md`.

